course: dictionary
lesson: 2303
title: Who is a critic?
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A critic is a person whose job is to give opinions about things like films, books, music, food, art or plays. Critics often write their opinions in newspapers, in magazines or online. «Critics and review sites give scores, but those are opinions, and your own taste may differ.»
explain: A critic can also be anyone who says what they think is wrong with a person, idea or plan. «Critics of the new rule» are people who say the rule is bad. Being a critic does not always mean being unkind; it means giving a reason for your opinion.
explain: Good critics write reviews with reasons. «Critics write reviews with reasons; you can read their reasons and still disagree, as taste is personal.» So a critic's opinion is one view, not the final answer. Ask yourself: what reasons are they giving?
fact: A critic is a person who gives opinions about films, books, music, food, art or plays.
fact: A critic can also be a person who says what is wrong with an idea, a plan or a rule.
fact: «Critic» is a noun, and the verb is «criticise» (UK) or «criticize» (US), which means to say what is wrong with something.
fact: «Critical thinking» means thinking carefully and fairly, not only being negative.
fact: «Your own worst critic» means someone who is very hard on themselves.
exercise: A film critic writes about films in newspapers and online. What is a critic's job? | *To give opinions about films, books, music, food, art or plays | To make films and books | To read the news aloud on the radio | To sell tickets at the cinema
exercise: «Critics of the new rule say it is unfair.» What does critics mean here? | People who are going to vote for the rule | People who agree with the rule and cheer for it | People who wrote the rule down in a book | *People who say what they think is wrong with the rule
exercise: «Everyone's a critic» is a joke. When do people say it? | When someone shares a photo of their dog | When someone asks you the time | When someone gives you a prize | *When someone complains about your work
test: Which word means to say what is wrong with something? | forget | *criticise | whisper | celebrate
test: «An inner critic is the mean voice in your head.» Is the inner critic always telling the truth? | Only when you are asleep | Only on Mondays | Yes, it always is | *No, it is not the truth
exam: «Critics write reviews with reasons; you can read their reasons and still disagree, as taste is personal.» What does this tell you about critics? | Their opinion is always the final answer | Taste is the same for everyone | *Their opinion is one view, and you can disagree with it | Critics never give reasons
